; Stage 15 W4c (design/stage15-stress-test/diagnostics.md §W4c).
; The accept criterion's shape: 8 nesting levels with ONE `)` missing from the
; closing run, so `defn main` never closes and the next top-level form is read
; as part of its body.
; Before: `unterminated list` at line 12 and nothing else. The innermost unclosed
;   form's opening line was already reported (the design doc's "reports where the
;   form starts" is accurate but incomplete) -- it says where the reader ran out
;   of input, not where the `)` went missing.
; After:  the same primary location PLUS the second number that localizes it:
;   line 23 opens a new top-level form in column 0 while a form is still open, so
;   the missing `)` is above line 23.
(defn main ():i32
  (let (v0:i32 0)
    (let (v1:i32 1)
      (let (v2:i32 2)
        (let (v3:i32 3)
          (let (v4:i32 4)
            (let (v5:i32 5)
              (let (v6:i32 6)
                (let (v7:i32 7)
                  (return v7)
))))))))
(defn other ():i32 (return 0))
